{"name":"Pouf of Pink","hex":"#decce4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pouf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A headdress for women popular in 18th century France. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A high hair style for women consisting of a roll or pad of hair, worn up."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make poufy or bouffant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pouf"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pouf","blocks":[{"text":"The pouf or pouffe, also \"toque\" is a hairstyle and a hairstyling support deriving from 18th-century France. It was made popular by the Queen of France, Marie Antoinette (1755–1793), when she wore it in June 1775 at the coronation of her husband Louis XVI, triggering a wave of French noblewomen to wear their hair in the same manner. The hairstyle would become popular across Europe in the 1770s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Marie-Antoinette%2C_1775_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Antoine_L%C3%A9cuyer.jpg/330px-Marie-Antoinette%2C_1775_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Antoine_L%C3%A9cuyer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pouf","wikidata":"Q7235474"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/After_Thomas_Gainsborough_%281727-88%29_-_Queen_Charlotte_%281744-1818%29_-_RCIN_403522_-_Royal_Collection.jpg/500px-After_Thomas_Gainsborough_%281727-88%29_-_Queen_Charlotte_%281744-1818%29_-_RCIN_403522_-_Royal_Collection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/After_Thomas_Gainsborough_%281727-88%29_-_Queen_Charlotte_%281744-1818%29_-_RCIN_403522_-_Royal_Collection.jpg/500px-After_Thomas_Gainsborough_%281727-88%29_-_Queen_Charlotte_%281744-1818%29_-_RCIN_403522_-_Royal_Collection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Queen Charlotte (1781)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAfter_Thomas_Gainsborough_(1727-88)_-_Queen_Charlotte_(1744-1818)_-_RCIN_403522_-_Royal_Collection.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4e/Stipple_engraving_of_Georgiana_Devonshire_after_Diana_Beauclerk.jpg/500px-Stipple_engraving_of_Georgiana_Devonshire_after_Diana_Beauclerk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4e/Stipple_engraving_of_Georgiana_Devonshire_after_Diana_Beauclerk.jpg/500px-Stipple_engraving_of_Georgiana_Devonshire_after_Diana_Beauclerk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Duchess of Devonshire (1782)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStipple_engraving_of_Georgiana_Devonshire_after_Diana_Beauclerk.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/L%C3%A9onard-Alexis_Auti%C3%A9_at_work_-_Bashor_2013_plate9.jpg/500px-L%C3%A9onard-Alexis_Auti%C3%A9_at_work_-_Bashor_2013_plate9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig